WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.775
Try it.

2
00:00:00.775 --> 00:00:05.812
Lab 1 runs in PowerShell 7, against
fixtures, and nothing signs in.

3
00:00:05.812 --> 00:00:13.000
Step one starts in the validation kit,
and runs VK-INT-07 on its fail fixture.

4
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.250
One GPO is imported.

5
00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:19.794
Two are targeted in Active Directory
with a readiness of partial or error,

6
00:00:19.794 --> 00:00:22.475
so they hold settings
Intune can't take over.

7
00:00:22.475 --> 00:00:23.737
Those are findings.

8
00:00:23.737 --> 00:00:27.988
An empty GPO is a warning:
confirm where its settings go.

9
00:00:27.988 --> 00:00:31.376
And one in-scope GPO was
never imported at all.

10
00:00:31.376 --> 00:00:36.834
Step two moves to the group policy folder,
and runs Microsoft's import sample twice,

11
00:00:36.834 --> 00:00:39.563
with the same file,
against the fake Graph.

12
00:00:39.563 --> 00:00:42.949
Now the tenant holds error
reporting and dumps twice,

13
00:00:42.949 --> 00:00:44.950
two policies with the same name.

14
00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:47.475
And the calls are two POSTs and no GET.

15
00:00:47.475 --> 00:00:49.010
The sample never looked.
